e ​Autism Center Toggle menu Our Services Our Staff Request More Information Fine Arts Center Toggle menu Box Office Upcoming Events and Exhibitions Fine Arts Center Facilities Regis Dental Center Event Planning and Facility Rentals Toggle menu Host your event at Regis Spaces for Rent Testimonials Request More Information Availability of Employees for Information Dissemination The Pride Faculty Lecture series began in 2020 as a forum to discuss how Regis, as a community, could both influence and be affected by systemic racism and the COVID-19 pandemic. Faculty lectures have explored how inequities are perpetuated and addressed locally, nationally, and globally against the backdrop of this health crisis. The 2022-2023 theme, Challenges and Change in Higher Education , asks faculty to reflect on how they work to understand and confront inequities in the context of higher education. We look forward to showcasing how Regis College faculty use their research and teaching to support our educational mission and act as agents of change in uncertain times. Spring 2023 Lecture Recordings March: Heritage Week Conversation: Our Mission, Our Values, Our Classrooms April: Challenges and Change In Higher Ed: Generative AI and ChatGPT Previous Lecture Recordings February 2022 Recording March 2021 Recording February 2021 Recording December 2020 Recording October 2020 Recording Regis College Footer menu SPIKE - Student Portal SHARP - Faculty/Staff Portal Weather Emergencies Website Feedback Footer middle menu Faculty and Staff Directory Working at Regis Emergency Information Title IX Resources Footer last menu Children's Center Events and Facility Rentals Fine Arts Center ​Administrative Offices 235 Wellesley Street, Weston MA 02493 781.768.7000 © 2026 Privacy Policy Footer social menu TikTok Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter Vimeo YouTube"
